      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Spontaneous Live Events Migration",
      "Anchor": "spontaneous-live-events-migration",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "We are consolidating our Live Events API around a single flow: Scheduled Live Events. Everything, whether the event will go live at a specific time or immediately, will now be created and managed under the scheduled live flow. We are retiring the spontaneous live events flow, moving to a single flow that gives everyone a consistent API surface and allows consolidation of logic around a single integration path.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What\u0027s Changing",
      "Anchor": "whats-changing",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What\u0027s Changing"
      ],
      "Text": "The Live Events API has historically supported two paths: spontaneous and scheduled. The scheduled flow is already the primary path for most of our creators. We are now standardizing on it for all use cases, regardless of when the event will go live.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What\u0027s Changing",
      "Anchor": "whats-changing",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What\u0027s Changing"
      ],
      "Text": "Going forward, only the scheduled live flow will be supported. You can use the same scheduled flow with scheduledAt set to 1 minute from now to provide continued support for the \u0022go live now\u0022 use case.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What\u0027s Changing",
      "Anchor": "whats-changing",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What\u0027s Changing"
      ],
      "Text": "The following table summarizes the key differences between the two flows:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
